\subsection{F6--F7: Interventions and Multiple Pathways}
\label{sec:f6}

\paragraph{F6: $\dt{=}1$ imagination does not prevent all collapse.}
Exp\_008e\_v3 restricts imagination to $\dt{=}1$ while retaining the trained embedding. Two of four seeds are healthy (s1: eval 869.9, $\nve = 0.94\times$; s4: eval 899.3, $\nve = 0.99\times$), while two collapse (50\%) via qualitatively distinct mechanisms (Figure~\ref{fig:multiple_pathways}). Seed~3 (Pathway~A) collapses via the CIVO mechanism with entropy decrease ($\nve = 4.02\times$, eval 92.7). Seed~2 (Pathway~B) collapses with \emph{increasing} entropy ($-5.21 \rightarrow -3.83$, $\nve = 3.78\times$, eval 137.2) while values remain stable. The bimodal outcome, with no intermediate states, confirms multiple independent vulnerability mechanisms. Pathway~B (008e\_v3\_s2) produces the sole non-CIVO false positive in the NVE classification.

